From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: fix bindir expansion during install

The install-exec-local rule spells the Automake bindir variable as
"($bindir)".  That text is appended to DESTDIR and passed unquoted to the
shell, so staged RPM installation fails on the unexpected opening
parenthesis.  Use the same $(bindir) expansion as the symlink rules below
it.  Update both the Automake source and the generated input shipped in the
release archive so the fix works without regenerating the build system.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI run 31768267502
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Remove-When: An upstream release ships the corrected bindir expansion.
---
 src/Makefile.am | 2 +-
 src/Makefile.in | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Makefile.am b/src/Makefile.am
--- a/src/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/Makefile.am
@@ -52 +52 @@ install-exec-local:
-	$(mkdir_p) $(DESTDIR)($bindir)
+	$(mkdir_p) $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)
diff --git a/src/Makefile.in b/src/Makefile.in
--- a/src/Makefile.in
+++ b/src/Makefile.in
@@ -1580 +1580 @@ install-exec-local:
-	$(mkdir_p) $(DESTDIR)($bindir)
+	$(mkdir_p) $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)
